    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a4">

                <pb facs="0313" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg241"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 350.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrows to Mr.
                            Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 19,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit here with copy
                    of the naturalization papers of John R. McCormack, an American suspect, at
                    present confined in Naas jail.</p>
                <p>Mr. McCormack wrote me from Clonmel jail, where he was then confined, on the 23d
                    February last, stating his case, and I replied to him the next day. His letter
                    to me and a copy of my reply are submitted herewith, together with Mr.
                    McCormack’s letter of April 18.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>B. H. BARROWS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
